// Every known competition instance: its curated competition group and the
// real name/type/era/dates it is created with.
//
// This runs in the BEFORE-other-importers phase, ahead of tools/import-bbl
// and tools/import-tp, because competitions.competition_group_id must already
// be correct when those tools run: tools/import-tp's awards import resolves a
// trophy by `${disambiguator}-${groupName}`, and the group name comes from
// the competition's own group. Classifying in the after-other-importers
// phase instead, once the source importers have already run, is too late.
//
// A create needs every NOT NULL column competitions has no default for --
// name, type, era_id and start_date -- so each entry carries real values,
// looked up from the same source data the real importers derive them from
// (BBL: the p=se name list and the p=ma&so=s match pages; TP: each
// competition directory's tournament_<slug>.json and match_*.json files),
// with the era resolved by the same rules bbl-competitions-import.service.ts
// and tp-competitions-import.service.ts use: an entry in an era's
// competitions.overrides in import-bbl-config.json5 pins that era and type,
// otherwise the first auto-assigning era whose [startDate, endDate) range
// contains the earliest match day wins. type follows the same rule both
// importers use -- a match-date span of at most 3 days is a cup, anything
// longer a season. eras.json5 in this directory exists so `era` has something
// to reference.
//
// These values are deliberately real, not placeholders: BBL's and TP's own
// competition upserts always set name, type, eraId, startDate and endDate
// unconditionally, so they overlay everything here on the next run -- but a
// competition that is never re-imported in some environment keeps what this
// file says, and a future reader should find the truth here. Neither importer
// ever sets competitionGroupId, so the classification survives untouched.
//
// The names here are the raw source names, except for the 36 instances the
// after-other-importers phase renames -- those carry their canonical name, so
// this file never creates a row under a name a later phase immediately
// replaces. Renaming itself stays in
// data/after-other-importers/competitions.json5: it can only run once the
// importers have created their rows with the raw source names.
//
// Source-data facts worth recording here: BBL's `s` id sequence has no s=9 at
// all -- not a gap in this file, it never existed on the source site.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', category: 'imported_data_source' },
    { name: 'tourplay.net', category: 'imported_data_source' },
    { name: 'Name', category: 'bookkeeping' },
  ],

  competitions: [
    // -- The Major Season track, seasons 1-18 (BBL, First era). BBL named
    // them plain "Season N" back when there was no Minor Season to
    // distinguish from, so the after-other-importers phase renames each to
    // the canonical "Major Season N" -- which is the name curated here, so
    // the row is never created under the raw name. The numeric id is the
    // competition's BBL `s` value from the p=se competition list -- the only
    // key competitions are matched by.
    {
      name: 'Major Season 1',
      type: 'season',
      era: { system: 'Name', id: 'First era' },
      startDate: '2011-09-09',
      endDate: '2011-12-18',
      competitionGroup: { system: 'Name', id: 'Major Season' },
      externalIds: [{ system: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', id: '1' }],
